<section class="wrap section section--flush" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
      <h2 id="problem-title">Visitors can't find answers your site already gives</h2>
      <ul class="quotes quotes--solo"><li><figure><blockquote><p>It cites, or it declines.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="cite"><strong>AnswerHatch</strong></figcaption></figure></li></ul>
    </div>
    <div class="copy">
      <p>Your site already answers most questions. People still ask things a website doesn't say directly: which form, which deadline, which address, which fee. They give up and email or call, and your team repeats what the site already publishes.</p>
      <p>The usual fix is an AI assistant. General-purpose assistants can invent an answer, and an invented answer about your organisation is a liability you will be asked to explain.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-mist" id="what" aria-labelledby="what-title">
